# DTF tier manifest: storage-prefix-rollup  (#2601, epic #2056 P2)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. The per-prefix rollup is materialized from
# the catalog tables and read via the repositories API; nothing here is
# backend-specific, so the default filesystem overlay suffices.
#
# The feature (#2601): a folder/path-tree storage usage rollup — a second
# materialization `repository_path_storage_stats` keyed by (repository, path
# prefix), refreshed with the existing storage-stats pass (schedule + GC), and
# a new endpoint GET /api/v1/repositories/{key}/storage/tree?prefix=&depth=.
#
# Oracle (oracle.sh) is the discriminating gate:
#   * create a repo, upload a nested file layout via the API, then POST
#     /api/v1/admin/storage-gc (the fix makes admin-triggered GC also refresh
#     the materialized stats, so the oracle has a deterministic trigger)
#   * GET .../storage/tree -> on the PRE-FIX image the route does not exist
#     (404) => RED. On the fixed image => 200 with correct per-prefix totals.
#   * assert nested-prefix rollup figures (root/libs/libs/app) and a dedup
#     case (one CAS object referenced from two subtrees: logical=3x,
#     physical=1x at the root; sum(children.physical) > root.physical).
#   * regression: the repo-level /storage endpoint (#2559 P1) still serves.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives a dozen API calls back-to-back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
